# cordis.yml.example — loading metavibe-dsh into a DeepSeek Harness deployment
#
# Recommended: load it as a PROFILE-LEVEL PLUGIN by inserting the row into the
# profile's cordis.patch.yml (`bash scripts/install.sh` does exactly this).
# The plugin then loads with the profile and its three READ-ONLY tools are
# available in every session — no agent preset to pick:
#
#   # <profile>/cordis.patch.yml
#   - insert:
#       - id: tool-metavibe
#         name: metavibe-dsh
#
# Alternative (per-session scoping): copy the row into ONE agent preset's
# `agent.cordis.yml` instead — the tools then appear only in sessions on that
# preset:
#
#   - id: tool-metavibe
#     name: metavibe-dsh
#
# metavibe-dsh publishes no service and needs no config — it only registers
# the three READ-ONLY knowledge tools (`metavibe_hub_list`,
# `metavibe_catalog_tree`, `metavibe_catalog_inspect`), consumes only the
# `tools` registry, and never touches the workspace.
